From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 17:00:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] ci: add publishing workflows (images, PyPI, sites) with
 configurable targets

- docker-build.yml: builds a package's image from its own folder and Dockerfile (symlinks materialized in the build context), tags and labels with docker/metadata-action, pushes to IMAGE_REGISTRY/IMAGE_NAMESPACE (repository variables).
- release.yml: for each package released by release-please, v<version> and latest images (api, federation-api, query-tool), bagel-cli-release.yml (PyPI upload, PYPI_REPOSITORY_URL selects the index, then the release image) and sites.yml.
- sites.yml: annotation-tool (main + beta) and query-tool on Netlify, only when SITE_DEPLOY is true; also runnable by hand for a released version.
- docker-nightly.yml: nightly images on push to main for the packages whose image inputs changed (dorny/paths-filter).
- images-validation.yml (temporary, migration validation): manual build and push of every image with a validation-<sha> tag.
- packages/bagel-cli/Dockerfile.nightly: one ARG so CI can pass the version computed from the bagel-cli-v* tags; the build context has no .git.
